# Codestral 25.08 — findings by Iceman

- Source: Mistral AI/Codestral 25.08 (Codestral 2508)
- Date: 2026-11-14 (UTC), deep second-pass research
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** Codestral 25.08 (Codestral 2508)
- **Short description:** Mistral AI’s specialized low-latency code model (July 2025 release/update) optimized for IDE autocomplete and fill-in-the-middle (FIM) completion, with chat/code assistance support and enterprise deployment options.
- **Provider / access:** Mistral AI (La Plateforme/API) and partner providers (e.g. OpenRouter). Mistral docs/models list `codestral-2508` / `codestral-latest`; local metadata lists `opencode/codestral-25.08`, `noFreeId`.
- **Release / knowledge:** Announced July 30, 2025 in Mistral’s “Codestral 25.08 and the Complete Mistral Coding Stack for Enterprise” post. Knowledge cutoff not explicitly stated in reviewed sources.
- **IDs:** `codestral-2508`, `codestral-latest` (Mistral), `mistralai/codestral-2508` (OpenRouter), `codestral-25.08` (local naming).
- **Context window:** 256,000 tokens context documented by Mistral docs/models and OpenRouter; max output varies by provider/API surface (OpenRouter advertises up to 32K max completion; local metadata notes 8,192 max out).
- **Modalities:** Text/code input and text/code output (completion and chat use cases).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-14):** ~$0.30 / $0.90 per 1M input/output tokens (Mistral/OpenRouter standard listings; provider-specific regional/pricing variants exist per OpenRouter).
- **Architecture:** Proprietary/specialized code model (Codestral family). Detailed architecture/parameter count not publicly disclosed in reviewed sources.

### Raw benchmarks found

> SECOND-PASS SELF-EXCLUSION (updated): Deep second-pass research using alternative web access (`webfetch`, PowerShell `Invoke-WebRequest`) reviewed Mistral’s announcement, Mistral docs/models/pricing, OpenRouter model page/docs, models.dev, and local metadata/prior report. Mistral reports relative/product and evaluation improvements (e.g. **+30% accepted completions**, **+10% retained code**, **50% fewer runaway generations** in live IDE usage; **+5% instruction following** on IF eval v8; **+5% average MultiplE** for code abilities) and positions Codestral for FIM/autocomplete and coding stack workflows. However, I did not find clearly extractable, independently verifiable standardized benchmark numerics for this exact model/version in the methodology categories used here (SWE-bench, Terminal-Bench, GPQA, AIME, LiveCodeBench, AA indices, etc.) attributable as comparable public scores. To avoid unverifiable or misattributed scoring, this file remains `.md.excluded` (notes only; scores ignored).

Agent / tool use:

- Primarily optimized for IDE autocomplete/FIM and developer-assistance workflows rather than autonomous multi-turn agent/tool-loop benchmarks. Terminal-Bench 2.1 / Tau2 / Tau3 / GDPval-AA / Toolathon / MCP-Atlas: **no verified public score found**.

Reasoning / knowledge:

- GPQA Diamond / HLE / AIME / AA Intelligence Index / LCR / CritPt: **no verified public score found**.

Coding:

- Reported improvements (Mistral announcement): +30% accepted completions, +10% retained code, 50% fewer runaway generations; +5% average MultiplE (chat/code abilities). These are relative/product/eval improvements, not directly comparable standardized benchmark scores in this project’s scoring framework.
- SWE-bench Verified / SWE-Pro / LiveCodeBench / SciCode / Vibe Code Bench: **no verified public score found**.

Long context:

- 256K context documented (Mistral docs/OpenRouter). No standalone long-context retrieval benchmark score found.

Multimodal:

- Text/code-focused model; no multimodal image/audio benchmark evidence found.

### Source comparison / conflicts

- **Specs/pricing:** Mistral docs, OpenRouter, and local metadata broadly align on Codestral 2508 identity as a 256K-context code model at ~$0.30/$0.90 per 1M tokens; max-output details differ by surface/provider (e.g. local metadata 8K vs OpenRouter-advertised higher completion limits).
- **Benchmarks/evidence:** Mistral provides relative/product metrics and some eval deltas (IF eval v8, MultiplE) but not clearly extractable standardized public benchmark numerics matching required categories for this exact version; AA model-detail page for this slug was not found (404).
- **Use-case fit:** Evidence supports strength in autocomplete/FIM and coding assistance; insufficient evidence for autonomous agent/tool-use and general reasoning/multimodal scoring in this framework.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

Not provided. Insufficient independently verifiable, clearly attributable standardized benchmark evidence for this exact model/version in the required scoring categories; no scored assessment is issued and this report remains self-excluded.

